WEBVTT

1
00:01:39.596 --> 00:01:41.826
<i>There comes a time</i>
<i>for every vampire... </i>

2
00:01:42.036 --> 00:01:47.030
<i>... when the idea of eternity becomes</i>
<i>momentarily unbearable. </i>

3
00:01:47.236 --> 00:01:51.275
<i>Living and feeding in the shadows</i>
<i>with only your own company... </i>

4
00:01:51.476 --> 00:01:55.355
<i>... rots into a solitary. </i>
<i>hollow existence. </i>

5
00:01:55.556 --> 00:01:58.024
<i>Immortality seems like a good idea... </i>

6
00:01:58.476 --> 00:02:02.151
<i>... until you realize</i>
<i>you're going to spend it alone. </i>

7
00:02:02.356 --> 00:02:06.713
<i>So I slept. hoping the sounds</i>
<i>of the passing eras would fade out... </i>

8
00:02:06.956 --> 00:02:09.072
<i>... and a sort of death might happen. </i>

9
00:02:09.276 --> 00:02:13.792
<i>But as I lay there. the world didn 't</i>
<i>sound like the place I had left... </i>

10
00:02:14.236 --> 00:02:17.387
<i>... but something different. </i>

11
00:02:17.876 --> 00:02:19.912
<i>Better... </i>

12
00:02:50.156 --> 00:02:55.276
<i>It became worthwhile to rise again</i>
<i>as new gods were born and worshiped. </i>

13
00:02:55.476 --> 00:02:58.513
<i>Night and day. they were never alone. </i>

14
00:02:58.716 --> 00:03:02.391
<i>I would become one of them. </i>

15
00:03:29.636 --> 00:03:33.675
<i>Whether it was the meal or</i>
<i>the 1 00 years of rest. I'm not sure. </i>

16
00:03:33.876 --> 00:03:37.107
<i>But suddenly</i>
<i>I was feeling better than ever. </i>

17
00:03:37.396 --> 00:03:39.432
<i>My senses so high... </i>

18
00:03:39.636 --> 00:03:44.232
<i>... they led me straight to the</i>
<i>instrument of my resurrection... </i>

19
00:03:44.436 --> 00:03:48.145
<i>... playing in my old house. </i>

20
00:04:16.036 --> 00:04:17.867
Jesus.

21
00:04:19.116 --> 00:04:20.629
Your voice... .

22
00:04:21.036 --> 00:04:22.435
Who the hell are you?

23
00:04:22.636 --> 00:04:26.868
<i>The question provoked</i>
<i>an irresistible urge. </i>

24
00:04:27.076 --> 00:04:29.874
l am the vampire Lestat.

25
00:04:30.076 --> 00:04:32.032
<i>It just rolled out of my mouth. </i>

26
00:04:32.236 --> 00:04:35.785
<i>With one sentence. </i>
<i>I betrayed everything about my kind. </i>

27
00:04:35.996 --> 00:04:37.907
<i>Betrayed our code of secrecy. </i>

28
00:04:38.116 --> 00:04:40.072
Vampire?

29
00:04:40.516 --> 00:04:43.713
- That's funny.
- Lndeed.

30
00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:46.305
Hilarious.

31
00:04:47.196 --> 00:04:49.073
You're all...

32
00:04:49.276 --> 00:04:50.914
...so beautiful.

33
00:04:51.476 --> 00:04:54.946
- Your hands are...
- Cold as death?

34
00:04:55.996 --> 00:04:58.066
- You're gonna kill us?
- No.

35
00:04:58.396 --> 00:05:02.992
All that you've ever dreamed of.
l'm going to make yours.

36
00:05:03.196 --> 00:05:05.710
This is your lucky day.

37
00:05:05.916 --> 00:05:08.191
<i>It was a bold move. I admit. </i>

38
00:05:08.436 --> 00:05:12.588
<i>But from that moment on they were</i>
<i>my friends. my children. my band. </i>

39
00:05:12.796 --> 00:05:16.232
<i>Giving the world a new god. </i>
<i>Me. </i>

40
00:07:02.796 --> 00:07:08.189
Okay. can l have your attention?
Okay. some questions. One at a time.

41
00:07:09.396 --> 00:07:11.785
- Yeah. you.
- So why here in London?

42
00:07:11.996 --> 00:07:14.510
We go where we're told to. like you.

43
00:07:14.716 --> 00:07:19.790
- How would you sum up your music?
- Sex. blood and rock and roll.

44
00:07:20.436 --> 00:07:21.994
Okay. excuse me.

45
00:07:23.276 --> 00:07:24.755
lt's time.

46
00:07:24.956 --> 00:07:26.548
May l present...

47
00:07:26.756 --> 00:07:30.271
...the vampire Lestat.

48
00:07:34.956 --> 00:07:36.150
<i>Good evening. </i>

49
00:07:37.636 --> 00:07:42.152
<i>Sorry I'm late. I was just trying</i>
<i>to catch my breakfast. </i>

50
00:07:44.796 --> 00:07:48.072
Okay. can we keep it short?
One at a time.

51
00:07:48.396 --> 00:07:49.545
Yeah. you.

52
00:07:49.956 --> 00:07:53.471
l may be wrong. but what
l remember about vampires is...

53
00:07:53.676 --> 00:07:56.634
...you generally keep
your identity secret.

54
00:07:56.836 --> 00:08:00.112
<i>Yes. But why hide it</i>
<i>in this day and age? </i>

55
00:08:00.316 --> 00:08:02.876
<i>I've hidden in the shadows</i>
<i>for centuries. </i>

56
00:08:03.076 --> 00:08:05.715
<i>It's time to share myself</i>
<i>with the world. </i>

57
00:08:06.236 --> 00:08:10.866
Could you prove it? You know. give us
a demonstration of your powers.

58
00:08:11.076 --> 00:08:16.104
<i>If you like. I can give you a private</i>
<i>demonstration in your hotel tonight. </i>

59
00:08:20.036 --> 00:08:24.188
Your first and only concert's
in Death Valley. just days away.

60
00:08:24.436 --> 00:08:27.712
- Why just the one?
- <i>I don 't like repeating myself. </i>

61
00:08:27.916 --> 00:08:32.546
There are rumors about
the hidden meaning in your lyrics...

62
00:08:32.756 --> 00:08:36.305
...that you're giving away
vampire secrets. Ls that true?

63
00:08:36.556 --> 00:08:41.710
<i>Maybe I'm trying to resurrect a few</i>
<i>old friends. Daring them to come out. </i>

64
00:08:41.916 --> 00:08:46.148
Won't these vampires be pissed off
that you're giving away secrets?

65
00:08:46.836 --> 00:08:49.987
<i>I imagine they are. yes. </i>

66
00:08:50.196 --> 00:08:53.666
Do you have anything to say
to the other vampires?

67
00:08:53.876 --> 00:08:56.788
<i>As a matter of fact. I do. </i>

68
00:08:58.316 --> 00:09:02.867
<i>Come out. come out. wherever you are. </i>

69
00:09:04.596 --> 00:09:08.066
<i>See you all in Death Valley. </i>

70
00:09:29.276 --> 00:09:33.792
l heard Lestat keeps all these girls
in his cellar. And it's nice.

71
00:09:33.996 --> 00:09:36.590
They give you food
and cable and weed.

72
00:09:36.796 --> 00:09:38.195
Oh. please.

73
00:09:38.436 --> 00:09:42.987
But you have to let him suck you
on your neck whenever he wants.

74
00:09:43.196 --> 00:09:46.233
- Doesn't sound too bad.
- Done worse.

75
00:09:46.436 --> 00:09:48.233
- L'll say.
- This way. girls.

76
00:10:01.236 --> 00:10:03.750
So this is Lestat's house?

77
00:10:03.956 --> 00:10:07.153
lt is this week. We move around a lot.

78
00:10:07.396 --> 00:10:08.795
Why is that?

79
00:10:09.476 --> 00:10:12.593
What can l say? The guy is just... .

80
00:10:14.116 --> 00:10:19.429
- Boss. L didn't see you there.
- No. You wouldn't. would you?

81
00:10:22.836 --> 00:10:26.112
These are the girls
that you asked for.

82
00:10:26.796 --> 00:10:28.275
Yes.

83
00:10:43.316 --> 00:10:46.353
Do you want me to take
the girls home later?

84
00:10:46.556 --> 00:10:48.626
No. thank you. Roger.

85
00:10:48.836 --> 00:10:51.430
l'll make sure they're taken care of.

86
00:10:54.036 --> 00:10:55.992
You want some?

87
00:10:56.956 --> 00:10:58.867
Want me?

88
00:10:59.876 --> 00:11:01.548
You hungry?

89
00:11:05.596 --> 00:11:08.952
You hungry for something else?

90
00:11:12.956 --> 00:11:14.674
Come on.

91
00:11:15.116 --> 00:11:18.472
- Don't you want to have some fun?
- Don't do that.

92
00:11:18.756 --> 00:11:20.986
Are you ticklish?

93
00:11:21.196 --> 00:11:23.756
l'm very ticklish.

94
00:12:27.116 --> 00:12:29.186
Come out. come out...

95
00:12:29.436 --> 00:12:31.745
...whoever you are.

96
00:12:39.636 --> 00:12:41.274
<i>Jesse. </i>

97
00:12:43.036 --> 00:12:46.073
<i>Jesse. </i>

98
00:12:46.276 --> 00:12:47.755
<i>A voice... </i>

99
00:12:48.676 --> 00:12:50.712
<i>... calling to me... </i>

100
00:12:50.916 --> 00:12:52.907
<i>... in my dreams. </i>

101
00:12:53.116 --> 00:12:56.631
<i>The same dream I've had</i>
<i>since I was 6.</i>

102
00:12:57.036 --> 00:12:59.755
<i>I have a family of my own. </i>

103
00:13:00.076 --> 00:13:02.636
<i>Not a strange dream. really. </i>

104
00:13:02.836 --> 00:13:05.430
<i>One every orphan has. </i>

105
00:13:32.076 --> 00:13:33.828
l'm sorry. but you must go.

106
00:13:34.036 --> 00:13:37.665
Why can't l stay with you?
Please. Aunt Maharet.

107
00:13:37.876 --> 00:13:41.186
l don't want you to go. But you must.

108
00:13:41.636 --> 00:13:44.355
Aunt. you're bleeding.

109
00:13:50.796 --> 00:13:52.673
You must be with your own.

110
00:13:52.876 --> 00:13:57.392
- <i>I knew things were not normal. </i>
- This isn't the life l wanted for you.

111
00:13:57.596 --> 00:14:01.509
<i>I only knew I was part of them. </i>
<i>and being cast out. </i>

112
00:14:01.716 --> 00:14:02.910
<i>Was I bad? </i>

113
00:14:03.116 --> 00:14:05.152
<i>Had I done something wrong? </i>

114
00:14:05.356 --> 00:14:07.711
l'll always be watching over you.

115
00:14:07.916 --> 00:14:10.271
l want to stay with you forever.

116
00:14:10.516 --> 00:14:12.905
You can't.

117
00:14:47.236 --> 00:14:49.352
<i>I'm Serena Altschul. MTV News. </i>

118
00:14:49.556 --> 00:14:54.266
<i>Vampire turned rocker Lestat</i>
<i>has returned with a new CD. </i> Forsaken.

119
00:14:54.476 --> 00:14:56.387
<i>Although from New Orleans... </i>

120
00:14:56.596 --> 00:14:59.986
<i>... he claims to be an 1 8th</i>-<i>century</i>
<i>French nobleman... </i>

121
00:15:00.196 --> 00:15:02.756
<i>... who has been asleep</i>
<i>for over 1 00 years. </i>

122
00:15:02.956 --> 00:15:08.553
<i>Here's a look at the new video</i>
<i>from the debut album. "Redeemer. "</i>

123
00:16:14.436 --> 00:16:17.075
<i>Like everyone. I assumed</i>
<i>Lestat was a joke. </i>

124
00:16:17.276 --> 00:16:22.191
A rock star with a gimmick. Then one
of his lyrics caught my attention.

125
00:16:22.516 --> 00:16:25.633
"Take a walk down the aisle
at the end of the mile.

126
00:16:25.836 --> 00:16:28.953
Give your life to my charms
in the Admiral's Arms. "

127
00:16:29.156 --> 00:16:30.635
That rang a bell.

128
00:16:30.836 --> 00:16:33.350
l tracked down old leases in London.

129
00:16:33.556 --> 00:16:37.549
lt turns out in the late 1 600s
there was a pub in Mile End...

130
00:16:37.756 --> 00:16:39.553
...called the Admiral's Arms.

131
00:16:39.756 --> 00:16:42.793
lt had a reputation for dealing
with black magic...

132
00:16:42.996 --> 00:16:45.464
...and reports of people vanishing.

133
00:16:45.676 --> 00:16:50.750
Here's where you could find
the Admiral's Arms in old London.

134
00:16:50.956 --> 00:16:53.834
That part of London
is mostly warehouses...

135
00:16:54.036 --> 00:16:57.995
...meat-packing plants and
a private club in the same location.

136
00:16:59.236 --> 00:17:02.592
l think that it's a vampire coven.

137
00:17:02.796 --> 00:17:05.435
And Lestat is leading us to it.

138
00:17:07.436 --> 00:17:10.394
- Who took this picture?
- L did.

139
00:17:10.596 --> 00:17:14.145
You're still an apprentice.
You don't do field work.

140
00:17:14.356 --> 00:17:15.914
The Talamasca has a code.

141
00:17:16.116 --> 00:17:19.586
l know. "Observe the dark realm.
but be not of it. "

142
00:17:19.796 --> 00:17:22.594
Well. it's held good for 1 2 centuries.

143
00:17:22.796 --> 00:17:26.550
We record and observe.
but never interfere.

144
00:17:26.756 --> 00:17:28.792
l had to see it for myself.

145
00:17:31.596 --> 00:17:33.666
ls David aware of this?

146
00:17:34.196 --> 00:17:35.185
Jesse?

147
00:17:37.636 --> 00:17:38.625
Hello. David.

148
00:17:39.396 --> 00:17:42.911
- L was explaining...
- Why don't you see me in my office?

149
00:17:46.036 --> 00:17:49.073
This is a real coven.
ln the middle of London.

150
00:17:49.276 --> 00:17:52.507
All the more reason
to have told me first.

151
00:17:54.076 --> 00:17:55.668
Listen. Jesse...

152
00:17:58.956 --> 00:18:01.470
...we know about Lestat.

153
00:18:01.876 --> 00:18:04.549
What he's doing is unprecedented.

154
00:18:05.516 --> 00:18:07.029
So why is he doing it?

155
00:18:07.236 --> 00:18:10.672
Aren't you curious?
Don't you think we should find out?

156
00:18:12.036 --> 00:18:14.106
Let me show you something.

157
00:18:17.076 --> 00:18:18.907
What do you see?

158
00:18:21.516 --> 00:18:24.030
Mid-1 500s. Florence.

159
00:18:25.116 --> 00:18:26.629
This one?

160
00:18:30.276 --> 00:18:33.188
- This man is in both.
- Yes.

161
00:18:35.476 --> 00:18:37.706
All the different paint samples...

162
00:18:38.396 --> 00:18:40.193
...all authentic.

163
00:18:40.396 --> 00:18:43.911
Each painted at the time
of their particular style.

164
00:18:50.196 --> 00:18:52.266
His name is Marius.

165
00:18:53.116 --> 00:18:55.835
l've been tracing him for years.

166
00:18:56.276 --> 00:18:58.267
My little obsession.

167
00:18:58.516 --> 00:19:01.508
The closest we've come
to the original vampire.

168
00:19:01.796 --> 00:19:05.266
Marius himself dates back to 400 B.C.

169
00:19:08.516 --> 00:19:10.871
So he's older than Lestat.

170
00:19:11.076 --> 00:19:13.146
He made Lestat.

171
00:19:13.836 --> 00:19:15.155
How do you know that?

172
00:19:15.396 --> 00:19:18.115
Because l have Lestat's journal.

173
00:19:21.396 --> 00:19:22.749
l want to see it.

174
00:19:24.996 --> 00:19:27.954
Promise me you'll never
go back to that place.

175
00:19:57.996 --> 00:20:01.306
<i>It was the winter of 1 788.</i>

176
00:20:01.516 --> 00:20:06.271
<i>And I was brought to a Mediterranean</i>
<i>island by the man who made me. </i>

177
00:20:07.596 --> 00:20:11.111
<i>If a man is what you'd call him. </i>

178
00:20:58.596 --> 00:21:00.905
Lestat. welcome.

179
00:21:02.916 --> 00:21:04.269
Who are you?

180
00:21:04.516 --> 00:21:06.347
Do l know you?

181
00:21:08.756 --> 00:21:12.465
l am unknowable by nature.
but you may call me Marius.

182
00:21:12.676 --> 00:21:17.306
l'm the lord of a great manor.
They'll send an army to look for me.

183
00:21:17.516 --> 00:21:20.428
l doubt they'll find you.
Lord de Lioncourt.

184
00:21:20.636 --> 00:21:22.547
You're a long way from home.

185
00:21:50.596 --> 00:21:52.109
You're weak...

186
00:21:52.636 --> 00:21:53.989
...near passing.

187
00:21:55.756 --> 00:21:58.270
l can barely hear your heartbeat.

188
00:21:59.356 --> 00:22:04.430
The future hastens.
An age beyond my antique reason.

189
00:22:04.636 --> 00:22:07.469
You will help me understand
these times.

190
00:22:07.836 --> 00:22:09.827
That's why l chose you.

191
00:22:10.196 --> 00:22:11.709
Chose me for what?

192
00:22:21.156 --> 00:22:22.555
Drink...

193
00:22:23.036 --> 00:22:24.594
...and live.

194
00:22:25.476 --> 00:22:28.593
You've been brave enough
for one night. my son.

195
00:22:31.236 --> 00:22:33.352
Drink...

196
00:22:34.756 --> 00:22:36.712
...and learn.

197
00:22:38.916 --> 00:22:41.430
Good. is it not?

198
00:22:45.076 --> 00:22:47.544
No more. No more. Lestat.

199
00:22:48.916 --> 00:22:50.713
No more!

200
00:23:23.636 --> 00:23:25.945
Don't be afraid.

201
00:23:26.196 --> 00:23:29.108
lt's only your body that dies.

202
00:23:42.996 --> 00:23:45.226
More.

203
00:23:47.516 --> 00:23:50.872
<i>I impressed my maker</i>
<i>with my thirst for things. </i>

204
00:23:51.076 --> 00:23:53.636
<i>He set out to educate me</i>
<i>in the unknown. </i>

205
00:23:53.836 --> 00:23:58.227
<i>Taught me all about the world. </i>
<i>its hidden history... </i>

206
00:23:58.476 --> 00:24:00.751
<i>... and about myself. </i>

207
00:24:05.956 --> 00:24:08.186
That's enough. my son.

208
00:24:10.956 --> 00:24:14.073
When you feed. hold back
from the moment of death.

209
00:24:14.276 --> 00:24:18.667
Never take the last drop. or it will
draw you in and you will die.

210
00:24:23.876 --> 00:24:26.106
Appreciate your prey.

211
00:24:31.036 --> 00:24:35.154
Their blood that we take into us
carries with it life...

212
00:24:35.396 --> 00:24:39.833
...their life. their knowledge.
their complexity.

213
00:24:42.756 --> 00:24:46.146
<i>My senses run amuck. </i>
<i>like a newborn child. </i>

214
00:24:46.956 --> 00:24:52.155
<i>And as for my new powers. I was beside</i>
<i>myself with the pleasure of it all. </i>

215
00:24:54.556 --> 00:24:56.148
We've stayed long enough.

216
00:24:56.396 --> 00:24:58.068
But we've spoken to no one.

217
00:24:58.596 --> 00:25:01.269
A vampire's life
is a life of discretion.

218
00:25:01.516 --> 00:25:02.995
Discretion?

219
00:25:03.636 --> 00:25:05.513
Why must we hide. Marius?

220
00:25:05.716 --> 00:25:08.913
We are the powerful.
we are the immortal.

221
00:25:09.116 --> 00:25:12.472
We should walk fearless
in the open. no?

222
00:25:22.716 --> 00:25:24.866
That cannot be.

223
00:25:25.836 --> 00:25:28.430
We're vulnerable during the day.

224
00:25:28.636 --> 00:25:32.629
Mortals must never know about us.
for the sake of all our kind.

225
00:25:33.076 --> 00:25:35.146
So l could never know her?

226
00:25:35.396 --> 00:25:37.591
Not unless you wanted to kill her.

227
00:25:44.596 --> 00:25:46.348
So l can never be known?

228
00:25:48.916 --> 00:25:51.589
You must be dead to the world.

229
00:25:52.756 --> 00:25:55.031
Come on. time to leave.

230
00:26:53.516 --> 00:26:55.666
Sophia. run! Run!

231
00:26:55.996 --> 00:26:58.305
Go! Go...

232
00:26:59.076 --> 00:27:00.304
Lestat...

233
00:27:00.516 --> 00:27:02.711
...stop her!

234
00:27:03.476 --> 00:27:04.465
You must!

235
00:27:40.556 --> 00:27:44.310
We must remain in the shadows.

236
00:27:45.636 --> 00:27:49.072
You still have a few
lingering mortal emotions.

237
00:27:50.116 --> 00:27:53.347
They'll serve you no good. my friend.

238
00:28:05.436 --> 00:28:07.233
Forgive me.

239
00:28:13.996 --> 00:28:19.832
<i>The faces of my victims haunted me. </i>
<i>reminding me of my fate. </i>

240
00:28:20.036 --> 00:28:22.266
<i>For nights and days I played... </i>

241
00:28:22.476 --> 00:28:27.948
<i>... furious that I would never partake</i>
<i>of the simple joys of the world. </i>

242
00:28:28.156 --> 00:28:30.306
<i>I was meant for more than this. </i>

243
00:29:08.316 --> 00:29:10.068
Marius?

244
00:30:28.156 --> 00:30:30.716
Would you like me to play for you?

245
00:32:52.636 --> 00:32:55.150
What have you done. Lestat?

246
00:33:04.076 --> 00:33:07.671
- More!
- L don't think so. my little lord.

247
00:33:07.876 --> 00:33:09.787
- Let me go.
- No.

248
00:33:09.996 --> 00:33:13.352
You've had the purest blood.
seen the oldest things.

249
00:33:13.556 --> 00:33:18.755
- Far too much for one as young as you.
- Her blood is like liquid fire.

250
00:33:18.956 --> 00:33:20.355
Who is she?

251
00:33:25.556 --> 00:33:27.547
She's your mother.

252
00:33:27.756 --> 00:33:29.712
She's my mother.

253
00:33:29.916 --> 00:33:33.909
Akasha. the queen of all
who are damned.

254
00:33:34.596 --> 00:33:36.427
And he's her king.

255
00:33:36.876 --> 00:33:41.825
Akasha and Enkil nearly drank this
earth dry when they ruled over Egypt.

256
00:33:42.036 --> 00:33:45.824
They drank until Enkil
lost his will to drink.

257
00:33:46.036 --> 00:33:50.746
Without her mate beside her. she also
lost hers. They became living statues.

258
00:33:50.956 --> 00:33:56.394
She respects nothing except the taste
of blood. human and immortal alike.

259
00:33:56.716 --> 00:33:58.195
No. Release me!

260
00:34:03.996 --> 00:34:06.305
She made you quite powerful.

261
00:34:06.516 --> 00:34:08.666
You'll not stop me!

262
00:34:09.836 --> 00:34:12.589
Can l hear her blood in your voice?

263
00:34:13.396 --> 00:34:16.752
ln all the years of my care.
not once have they moved.

264
00:34:16.956 --> 00:34:20.505
Until tonight. And she chose me.

265
00:34:21.396 --> 00:34:22.909
l chose you.

266
00:34:26.796 --> 00:34:29.993
Where are you going?! Marius!

267
00:35:25.076 --> 00:35:31.151
<i>Many times since. I have called</i>
<i>to Marius. But there was no answer. </i>

268
00:35:31.716 --> 00:35:35.948
<i>Just the endless procession</i>
<i>of days. months... </i>

269
00:35:36.156 --> 00:35:37.635
<i>... years. </i>

270
00:35:38.716 --> 00:35:42.231
<i>My teacher left me</i>
<i>to my darkest lesson. </i>

271
00:35:42.436 --> 00:35:44.506
<i>That in the end. we are alone. </i>

272
00:35:45.356 --> 00:35:51.067
<i>And there is nothing but the cold. </i>
<i>dark wasteland of eternity. </i>

273
00:36:14.956 --> 00:36:18.312
<i>David thought the journal</i>
<i>would satisfy my curiosity. </i>

274
00:36:18.916 --> 00:36:21.953
<i>But it only made me want</i>
<i>to know more. </i>

275
00:36:22.156 --> 00:36:24.716
<i>I had to go back</i>
<i>to the Admiral's Arms. </i>

276
00:36:24.916 --> 00:36:27.225
<i>I had no choice. </i>

277
00:37:02.236 --> 00:37:05.114
<i>This is a fantastic place. I love it. </i>

278
00:37:05.756 --> 00:37:08.475
You sure l can't get you a drink?

279
00:37:09.396 --> 00:37:10.590
Soon.

280
00:38:10.716 --> 00:38:12.195
Hi.

281
00:38:13.036 --> 00:38:14.435
- Hi.
- Come here often?

282
00:38:14.796 --> 00:38:16.468
All the time.

283
00:38:20.156 --> 00:38:22.875
l don't see any marks.

284
00:38:23.076 --> 00:38:25.510
You haven't seen the rest of my body.

285
00:38:26.516 --> 00:38:28.950
ls that an invitation?

286
00:38:29.156 --> 00:38:31.192
Sorry. l'm taken.

287
00:38:31.396 --> 00:38:33.114
And...

288
00:38:33.756 --> 00:38:35.747
...where is your host?

289
00:38:36.156 --> 00:38:37.475
He's here somewhere.

290
00:38:40.996 --> 00:38:44.511
This host. what's his name?

291
00:38:48.356 --> 00:38:49.630
Marius.

292
00:38:50.436 --> 00:38:53.030
Sorry. don't know the guy.

293
00:38:53.236 --> 00:38:57.434
- Of course not. He's an ancient.
- There aren't any ancients left.

294
00:38:57.636 --> 00:39:00.196
They all turned to dust.

295
00:39:00.556 --> 00:39:03.628
So unless you've got him in a bottle
somewhere... .

296
00:39:03.836 --> 00:39:06.714
You're brave to joke.
l wish you could meet him.

297
00:39:06.916 --> 00:39:10.431
- And why is that?
- Because you might learn something.

298
00:39:13.716 --> 00:39:15.672
Excuse me.

299
00:39:29.436 --> 00:39:31.028
Going somewhere?

300
00:39:32.876 --> 00:39:35.754
Now this will only hurt a little bit.

301
00:39:36.116 --> 00:39:39.791
ln fact. you might even enjoy it.

302
00:39:39.996 --> 00:39:40.951
Don't do this.

303
00:40:00.756 --> 00:40:02.189
Boo.

304
00:40:17.116 --> 00:40:20.347
That was quite a performance.

305
00:40:20.956 --> 00:40:23.629
You should be more careful.

306
00:40:24.676 --> 00:40:27.827
- Thanks.
- For what?

307
00:40:28.156 --> 00:40:29.908
You saved me.

308
00:40:30.596 --> 00:40:32.507
How presumptuous.

309
00:40:33.356 --> 00:40:36.746
So you know Marius?

310
00:40:38.916 --> 00:40:40.508
l know a lot of things.

311
00:40:40.716 --> 00:40:43.310
Not how to stay alive. apparently.

312
00:40:43.596 --> 00:40:45.666
l guess we have that in common.

313
00:40:46.196 --> 00:40:48.994
Although l'm a little ahead
of the race here.

314
00:40:49.196 --> 00:40:51.664
Well. l can fix that.

315
00:40:52.236 --> 00:40:56.388
Your song "Redeemer" is about
the girl with the violin. Lsn't it?

316
00:40:58.036 --> 00:40:59.151
Yeah.

317
00:40:59.396 --> 00:41:00.749
ls it?

318
00:41:03.556 --> 00:41:05.751
What else do you think you know?

319
00:41:06.796 --> 00:41:07.990
l... .

320
00:41:08.196 --> 00:41:10.551
You're shaking.

321
00:41:10.756 --> 00:41:12.109
Cold.

322
00:41:13.076 --> 00:41:14.555
Still cold?

323
00:41:16.076 --> 00:41:19.830
Go on. Tell me more about me.

324
00:41:20.076 --> 00:41:21.634
You want... .

325
00:41:21.836 --> 00:41:23.713
What do l want?

326
00:41:25.036 --> 00:41:28.346
- You yearn.
- What do l yearn?

327
00:41:31.596 --> 00:41:34.235
For what do l yearn?

328
00:41:34.436 --> 00:41:36.472
To walk with the living.

329
00:41:37.956 --> 00:41:42.234
Out of the cold.
dark wasteland of eternity.

330
00:41:45.636 --> 00:41:46.625
Well...

331
00:41:48.956 --> 00:41:52.153
...that makes you
a very clever librarian.

332
00:41:52.356 --> 00:41:54.745
Talamasca.

333
00:41:54.956 --> 00:41:58.346
l knew l left that journal somewhere.

334
00:42:01.036 --> 00:42:04.790
- Was it a good read?
- Lt touched me.

335
00:42:05.356 --> 00:42:06.914
Did it. now?

336
00:42:08.356 --> 00:42:10.074
Don't worry. Jesse.

337
00:42:10.556 --> 00:42:12.990
Your kind never satisfies my thirst.

338
00:42:15.876 --> 00:42:19.107
Lestat. l know something
that's not in your journal.

339
00:42:21.596 --> 00:42:22.585
What?

340
00:42:23.036 --> 00:42:25.391
You still have the violin. don't you?

341
00:42:26.036 --> 00:42:27.992
No. l understand.

342
00:42:28.916 --> 00:42:30.588
After all. it's only human.

343
00:43:24.956 --> 00:43:26.867
Clever librarian.

344
00:43:36.676 --> 00:43:40.430
David. listen. l'm going
to Los Angeles for the concert.

345
00:43:41.076 --> 00:43:43.988
<i>I met him. David. I talked to Lestat. </i>

346
00:43:44.316 --> 00:43:46.386
What? Jesse?

347
00:43:46.596 --> 00:43:49.986
Listen to me very carefully now.

348
00:43:51.596 --> 00:43:54.349
You are no longer seeing
things clearly.

349
00:43:54.636 --> 00:43:58.265
<i>Lestat told the world that vampires</i>
<i>live among us. They're mad. </i>

350
00:43:58.476 --> 00:44:02.754
<i>They'll be at the concert to kill him. </i>
<i>You've become obsessed with it. </i>

351
00:44:02.956 --> 00:44:07.552
- <i>I'm worried about you. </i>
- Don't worry about me. L'll be okay.

352
00:44:07.756 --> 00:44:09.553
l'll check in and... .

353
00:44:10.556 --> 00:44:12.114
l'm sorry. L have to go.

354
00:44:12.316 --> 00:44:13.829
No. Jesse...

355
00:44:29.996 --> 00:44:33.784
<i>The city of Lost Angels already</i>
<i>fed on the blood of youth. </i>

356
00:44:33.996 --> 00:44:37.068
<i>My presence here barely</i>
<i>stirred a ripple. </i>

357
00:44:37.276 --> 00:44:39.585
<i>We had three days till the concert. </i>

358
00:44:39.796 --> 00:44:42.185
<i>I could feel something was coming. </i>

359
00:44:42.396 --> 00:44:45.433
<i>I just couldn 't figure out what. </i>

360
00:45:16.916 --> 00:45:18.395
Marius.

361
00:45:29.916 --> 00:45:31.634
Lestat.

362
00:45:32.956 --> 00:45:35.265
lt is good to see you. Lestat.

363
00:45:36.596 --> 00:45:37.824
And you.

364
00:45:38.076 --> 00:45:41.591
Still wearing the old fashions. l see.

365
00:45:43.276 --> 00:45:45.392
Old habits die hard.

366
00:45:45.596 --> 00:45:50.511
How did you manage to slip
through the '50s in red velvet?

367
00:45:51.156 --> 00:45:52.589
l slept.

368
00:45:53.876 --> 00:45:56.071
Don't think you missed much.

369
00:45:57.196 --> 00:46:00.745
- Elvis.
- Elvis. yes.

370
00:46:02.876 --> 00:46:04.867
You're bigger than he is now.

371
00:46:05.196 --> 00:46:06.185
So... .

372
00:46:07.036 --> 00:46:09.072
After all this time...

373
00:46:09.596 --> 00:46:11.427
...what's the occasion?

374
00:46:11.636 --> 00:46:16.915
You've just become very hard to avoid
these days. at least in conversation.

375
00:46:17.876 --> 00:46:21.266
- What are you trying to prove. Lestat?
- Oh. please.

376
00:46:21.476 --> 00:46:25.469
lt's a little too late to come over
all paternal now. Marius.

377
00:46:25.676 --> 00:46:29.305
Two hundred years
and not a word from you.

378
00:46:30.516 --> 00:46:33.508
You almost cost me everything.

379
00:46:36.276 --> 00:46:37.834
Now you've done it again.

380
00:46:38.476 --> 00:46:41.832
This isn't the time to settle
old scores.

381
00:46:43.476 --> 00:46:46.388
Vampires don't settle old scores.

382
00:46:48.436 --> 00:46:50.711
We harbor them.

383
00:46:54.876 --> 00:46:56.594
How did you find me?

384
00:46:57.076 --> 00:46:58.429
l made you.

385
00:46:58.716 --> 00:47:00.946
l've always known where you are.

386
00:47:01.756 --> 00:47:03.109
Besides...

387
00:47:03.476 --> 00:47:07.594
...l just had to look for the most
gauche house on the block.

388
00:47:09.156 --> 00:47:12.785
Come. Let me show you what it means
to live in the light.

389
00:47:22.436 --> 00:47:23.630
lmpressive.

390
00:47:23.836 --> 00:47:28.034
Reminds me of old mad druids
running around chanting in the forest.

391
00:47:28.236 --> 00:47:30.227
A return to the primitive.

392
00:47:30.836 --> 00:47:32.792
Out there. my fans...

393
00:47:34.036 --> 00:47:35.594
...they worship me.

394
00:47:35.956 --> 00:47:40.871
Millions of arms reach out to embrace.
beg me to come into their lives.

395
00:47:41.076 --> 00:47:42.953
lt's what you always wanted.

396
00:47:43.156 --> 00:47:45.716
With all my black little heart.

397
00:47:46.996 --> 00:47:50.193
Did you think of anyone but yourself?

398
00:47:50.596 --> 00:47:53.747
l only have myself.
You taught me that.

399
00:47:54.436 --> 00:47:57.667
lt may be time to get ready
for some company.

400
00:47:57.876 --> 00:48:03.269
- What's that supposed to mean?
- Your music's woken an old friend.

401
00:48:05.116 --> 00:48:06.674
Can't you hear it?

402
00:48:07.156 --> 00:48:10.592
Or is the applause all you
can hear now?

403
00:48:28.916 --> 00:48:30.190
Akasha.

404
00:48:30.956 --> 00:48:32.548
Arisen.

405
00:48:33.156 --> 00:48:35.875
She has taken the king's blood.

406
00:48:36.076 --> 00:48:37.907
Absorbed his power.

407
00:48:38.516 --> 00:48:41.508
Good. Let her come.

408
00:48:41.796 --> 00:48:43.866
Cancel the concert.

409
00:48:44.156 --> 00:48:45.475
Never.

410
00:48:45.996 --> 00:48:49.784
You're no match for her. Lestat.
You're not a god.

411
00:48:50.476 --> 00:48:53.149
We were once mortals too.

412
00:48:54.116 --> 00:48:56.789
lt is our heritage we protect.

413
00:48:56.996 --> 00:48:59.669
Such reverence for mortals.

414
00:48:59.876 --> 00:49:02.754
Then you should have left me as one.

415
00:50:00.956 --> 00:50:06.076
Scent is fading.
He was here too long ago.

416
00:50:06.276 --> 00:50:07.914
You like him. do you?

417
00:50:08.996 --> 00:50:10.952
He reminds me of someone.

418
00:50:11.156 --> 00:50:15.672
All he's going to remind you of soon
is a pile of bones.

419
00:50:15.876 --> 00:50:18.868
We're going to dismember him.
Bleed him dry.

420
00:50:19.076 --> 00:50:20.191
Really?

421
00:50:21.436 --> 00:50:24.712
ls that what you're going to do?

422
00:53:15.716 --> 00:53:19.072
<i>Old gods on new streets. </i>

423
00:53:19.556 --> 00:53:22.866
<i>Not only had the concert sold out</i>
<i>among the living... </i>

424
00:53:23.076 --> 00:53:26.068
<i>... it seemed all the undead</i>
<i>were coming too. </i>

425
00:53:26.276 --> 00:53:28.995
<i>There would be angry vampires</i>
<i>out there... </i>

426
00:53:29.196 --> 00:53:33.189
<i>... frightened of the light I was</i>
<i>directing on all our kind. </i>

427
00:53:33.436 --> 00:53:36.792
<i>Do you have anything to say</i>
<i>to the other vampires? </i>

428
00:53:36.996 --> 00:53:40.671
<i>Yes. as a matter of fact. I do. </i>

429
00:53:41.596 --> 00:53:44.827
<i>Come out. come out. wherever you are. </i>

430
00:53:45.596 --> 00:53:47.552
<i>They wanted me dead. </i>

431
00:53:47.756 --> 00:53:49.394
<i>Let them try. </i>

432
00:53:49.716 --> 00:53:51.115
<i>Bring it on. </i>

433
00:53:51.516 --> 00:53:54.189
<i>Better dead than alone. </i>

434
00:54:09.236 --> 00:54:11.670
Hey. honey. Want tickets for tomorrow?

435
00:54:11.876 --> 00:54:13.594
- Going to the show?
- No.

436
00:54:13.796 --> 00:54:17.345
- Come on. l got them for $200.
- $200?! L don't think so.

437
00:54:17.556 --> 00:54:23.188
- What if l say 1 50?
- 1 50? You're gonna cut me a deal?

438
00:54:23.436 --> 00:54:27.429
So. listen. just two girls. okay?
So how old are you again?

439
00:54:30.276 --> 00:54:33.427
- Check it out. Champagne?
- Yeah.

440
00:54:49.876 --> 00:54:54.791
Oh. my God. l can't believe
it's really you! L'm your biggest fan.

441
00:54:56.756 --> 00:54:58.075
Boo.

442
00:54:58.996 --> 00:55:00.224
Boo back.

443
00:55:01.116 --> 00:55:03.630
Lestat. l came all the way
from Tarzana.

444
00:55:03.836 --> 00:55:04.871
Really?

445
00:55:05.836 --> 00:55:07.428
- And you?
- London.

446
00:55:08.636 --> 00:55:11.070
A London Goth. L see.

447
00:55:12.156 --> 00:55:16.672
lt's funny. l would have pegged you
for a Talamascan.

448
00:55:17.596 --> 00:55:19.393
Maybe in another life.

449
00:55:19.596 --> 00:55:21.154
l'm an Episcopalian.

450
00:55:21.636 --> 00:55:24.946
And l'm a frigging Buddhist.
Lestat... .

451
00:55:25.156 --> 00:55:29.308
Roger. would you take our little
Episcopalian back to church?

452
00:55:29.516 --> 00:55:31.905
Just the one tonight? Sure.

453
00:55:32.116 --> 00:55:35.233
- Sweetheart. come on.
- What?

454
00:55:35.876 --> 00:55:37.468
- Come on.
- What?!

455
00:55:37.676 --> 00:55:40.713
- Lt's a good thing.
- Can l still go backstage?

456
00:55:42.396 --> 00:55:44.830
Why are you following me?

457
00:55:45.076 --> 00:55:46.475
What do you want?

458
00:55:59.396 --> 00:56:03.548
So you come all this way
just to return this to me?

459
00:56:03.756 --> 00:56:06.554
Out of the goodness of your heart?

460
00:56:09.116 --> 00:56:11.676
l want you to show me what it's like.

461
00:56:12.036 --> 00:56:15.028
What what is like. exactly?

462
00:56:15.236 --> 00:56:17.352
To be like you.

463
00:56:20.196 --> 00:56:22.232
l don't have time for this.

464
00:56:22.596 --> 00:56:26.669
- All a vampire has is time.
- Not this one.

465
00:56:28.556 --> 00:56:29.705
Right.

466
00:56:29.956 --> 00:56:32.516
The covens are coming for you.

467
00:56:32.716 --> 00:56:37.187
How are you going to spend your last
night. as you always have. alone?

468
00:56:37.396 --> 00:56:38.545
Why not?

469
00:56:39.236 --> 00:56:41.545
Why not share it with me?

470
00:56:45.276 --> 00:56:46.709
All right.

471
00:56:49.356 --> 00:56:52.553
This may be painful for a mortal.

472
00:56:52.756 --> 00:56:55.793
You're still attached to your skin.

473
00:56:56.796 --> 00:56:58.434
l don't care.

474
00:57:00.916 --> 00:57:02.668
Do you trust me?

475
00:57:06.276 --> 00:57:07.755
Yes.

476
00:57:16.556 --> 00:57:18.786
Then close your eyes.

477
00:58:32.996 --> 00:58:34.873
Marius was right.

478
00:58:35.076 --> 00:58:38.113
But l never understood
until l met you.

479
00:58:38.716 --> 00:58:40.627
What do you mean?

480
00:58:40.836 --> 00:58:43.987
You're beautiful to me
because you're human.

481
00:58:44.196 --> 00:58:46.266
Your frailty...

482
00:58:46.516 --> 00:58:48.393
...your short years...

483
00:58:50.716 --> 00:58:52.354
...your heart...

484
00:58:52.556 --> 00:58:55.229
...even as you think it's breaking.

485
00:58:59.436 --> 00:59:01.154
All that...

486
00:59:02.516 --> 00:59:06.987
...seems suddenly more precious
than anything l have ever known.

487
00:59:10.116 --> 00:59:12.835
l'm not as precious as you think.

488
00:59:21.916 --> 00:59:23.269
Do it.

489
00:59:26.756 --> 00:59:28.155
Please.

490
00:59:34.156 --> 00:59:36.351
Let me be with you.

491
00:59:38.516 --> 00:59:40.984
Let me know everything.

492
00:59:48.796 --> 00:59:51.230
You want to know everything?

493
00:59:53.236 --> 00:59:54.749
Come. then.

494
00:59:55.036 --> 00:59:56.788
l'll show you.

495
01:00:18.276 --> 01:00:20.665
What is it? What are we doing...?

496
01:01:04.636 --> 01:01:06.115
ls she all right?

497
01:01:10.276 --> 01:01:13.348
Get away! Get off me!

498
01:01:21.636 --> 01:01:23.228
Now you see?

499
01:01:23.756 --> 01:01:25.109
Are you ready?

500
01:01:26.836 --> 01:01:29.953
Now do you want it. huh?

501
01:01:32.916 --> 01:01:33.985
No.

502
01:01:34.436 --> 01:01:36.996
Of course you don't.

503
01:02:33.836 --> 01:02:36.509
They're pretty worked-up.
How you feeling?

504
01:02:36.716 --> 01:02:38.388
Hey. girls. come on!

505
01:02:39.556 --> 01:02:42.628
Okay. through here. Let him through!

506
01:02:42.996 --> 01:02:44.349
Back off. fella!

507
01:02:44.556 --> 01:02:45.909
Come on. children.

508
01:02:46.116 --> 01:02:48.186
Okay. guys. Come on!

509
01:02:50.436 --> 01:02:52.392
Let him through.

510
01:02:57.676 --> 01:02:59.029
Jesse!

511
01:03:01.556 --> 01:03:02.750
Jesse!

512
01:03:06.476 --> 01:03:07.875
Hello. David.

513
01:03:08.956 --> 01:03:12.153
l must show you my new
paintings sometime.

514
01:05:29.476 --> 01:05:30.591
Find Jesse.

515
01:06:17.036 --> 01:06:18.913
You want more?

516
01:06:22.236 --> 01:06:26.468
This one's for those
who've come for me.

517
01:09:18.876 --> 01:09:20.070
Akasha.

518
01:10:36.516 --> 01:10:38.472
Akasha?!

519
01:10:39.036 --> 01:10:41.470
Why so surprised. my love?

520
01:10:42.236 --> 01:10:44.192
You called. l have come.

521
01:10:45.236 --> 01:10:46.271
My love?

522
01:10:46.756 --> 01:10:49.190
Never fear me. Lestat.

523
01:10:50.236 --> 01:10:52.352
All your wishes have come true.

524
01:10:52.556 --> 01:10:54.114
My wishes?

525
01:10:56.236 --> 01:10:59.706
For a companion to share eternity.

526
01:11:02.116 --> 01:11:05.825
You're bold. like your music.

527
01:11:07.636 --> 01:11:12.391
You live your life in the open.
like l did long ago...

528
01:11:13.476 --> 01:11:15.194
...when l had a king.

529
01:11:15.716 --> 01:11:16.785
Had a king?

530
01:11:17.196 --> 01:11:18.834
He's no more.

531
01:11:19.596 --> 01:11:22.906
Now you are my consort.

532
01:11:23.836 --> 01:11:25.906
That's why l kept you safe.

533
01:11:26.996 --> 01:11:28.509
Alive.

534
01:11:29.436 --> 01:11:30.869
You?

535
01:11:32.556 --> 01:11:35.229
You thought it was all you?

536
01:11:38.236 --> 01:11:41.148
The ego of a king as well.

537
01:11:41.396 --> 01:11:42.829
Yes.

538
01:11:44.036 --> 01:11:47.233
l know you. Lestat.

539
01:11:47.636 --> 01:11:51.549
l know that you crave to have
the world at your feet.

540
01:11:52.956 --> 01:11:56.266
And l have come to give it to you.

541
01:11:58.116 --> 01:12:00.027
Where are we?

542
01:12:00.836 --> 01:12:02.713
<i>We are home. </i>

543
01:12:03.236 --> 01:12:08.264
<i>We live everywhere</i>
<i>and anywhere we choose. </i>

544
01:12:08.676 --> 01:12:12.225
<i>The world is our garden. </i>

545
01:14:31.116 --> 01:14:35.075
<i>All these years I'd hoped</i>
<i>this place was real. </i>

546
01:14:37.156 --> 01:14:42.276
<i>For the first time in my life. </i>
<i>I feel like I'm home. </i>

547
01:14:42.836 --> 01:14:46.715
<i>Strange that this journey</i>
<i>should lead me here. </i>

548
01:14:46.916 --> 01:14:50.033
<i>This place that's haunted my dreams. </i>

549
01:14:55.196 --> 01:14:57.915
<i>Aunt. you're bleeding. </i>

550
01:14:58.116 --> 01:15:00.232
<i>You must be with your own. </i>

551
01:15:02.756 --> 01:15:05.145
<i>I'll always be watching over you. </i>

552
01:15:05.396 --> 01:15:07.990
<i>I want to stay with you forever. </i>

553
01:15:09.156 --> 01:15:11.545
Forever is a very long time.

554
01:15:14.756 --> 01:15:16.348
Aunt Maharet.

555
01:15:25.956 --> 01:15:29.392
You haven't aged.
you haven't changed at all.

556
01:15:32.196 --> 01:15:34.471
l was once a mortal too.

557
01:15:34.756 --> 01:15:38.669
l bore a child before Akasha took me.
l took care of that child...

558
01:15:38.876 --> 01:15:42.425
...and her children.
and her children's children.

559
01:15:42.916 --> 01:15:45.066
This is our family.

560
01:15:45.276 --> 01:15:47.744
My way of coping with eternity.

561
01:15:49.716 --> 01:15:54.346
You are what keeps me connected
to the world of the living.

562
01:15:54.956 --> 01:15:58.915
When your parents died. l brought
you here to take care of you.

563
01:16:04.196 --> 01:16:06.869
Now is not the time.

564
01:16:08.196 --> 01:16:11.825
You were seeking answers
and now you've found them.

565
01:16:12.196 --> 01:16:15.791
The family is who you are.

566
01:17:43.076 --> 01:17:47.035
Drinking my blood allows you
to live in the light.

567
01:17:47.236 --> 01:17:51.991
And soon the sun will no longer
sting your eyes.

568
01:17:53.156 --> 01:17:57.513
This is but a taste
of what we shall share. my love.

569
01:17:58.556 --> 01:18:00.194
My king...

570
01:18:00.996 --> 01:18:03.749
...behold our kingdom.

571
01:18:04.396 --> 01:18:06.671
A kingdom of corpses?

572
01:18:08.596 --> 01:18:11.872
- Why?
- Why not?

573
01:18:12.516 --> 01:18:14.188
This is why you have risen?

574
01:18:14.396 --> 01:18:17.593
They believed in nothing.

575
01:18:17.956 --> 01:18:19.469
Now they are nothing.

576
01:18:25.836 --> 01:18:28.794
But you and l.
we will change all that.

577
01:18:29.956 --> 01:18:34.472
We will give the world something
to believe in again.

578
01:18:35.596 --> 01:18:37.587
Now come. my love.

579
01:18:37.956 --> 01:18:39.947
We have a score to settle.

580
01:18:51.596 --> 01:18:54.110
Since my mortal death.
l have watched...

581
01:18:54.796 --> 01:18:58.914
...l have guided and cared
for my human family...

582
01:18:59.436 --> 01:19:02.189
...generations beyond memory.

583
01:19:04.196 --> 01:19:07.711
This is why we must fight Akasha.

584
01:19:08.996 --> 01:19:13.626
- For the sake of your great family.
- The world we know is about to end.

585
01:19:13.956 --> 01:19:17.790
The only way to prevent this
is through Akasha's destruction.

586
01:19:17.996 --> 01:19:19.429
But how?

587
01:19:19.996 --> 01:19:22.464
When she gives blood.
she's vulnerable.

588
01:19:22.676 --> 01:19:26.430
Whoever takes the last of her blood
will not survive it.

589
01:19:26.636 --> 01:19:28.194
What about Lestat?

590
01:19:28.396 --> 01:19:34.107
Lestat has joined with Akasha.
He's lost to us now. Forget him.

591
01:19:55.876 --> 01:19:57.389
My children.

592
01:19:59.476 --> 01:20:02.468
lt warms my blood
to see you all gathered...

593
01:20:02.916 --> 01:20:04.429
...plotting against me.

594
01:20:04.636 --> 01:20:06.945
- Akasha.
- Maharet.

595
01:20:07.756 --> 01:20:12.386
- You will address my king first.
- Lestat. what has she done to you?

596
01:20:14.916 --> 01:20:17.350
Lestat. step aside.

597
01:20:17.796 --> 01:20:18.706
Never.

598
01:20:18.916 --> 01:20:21.476
The world has changed
since you reigned.

599
01:20:21.676 --> 01:20:23.746
Then we shall change it back.

600
01:20:24.036 --> 01:20:26.106
Humans are animals...

601
01:20:26.756 --> 01:20:28.667
...brute creatures.

602
01:20:28.876 --> 01:20:33.825
- Their destruction can only make sense.
- We've found other ways to coexist.

603
01:20:34.036 --> 01:20:38.234
ln silence! Ln shadows and shame!
And for what?

604
01:20:38.436 --> 01:20:40.347
For respect of mortals?

605
01:20:40.556 --> 01:20:42.547
They are nothing to us.

606
01:20:42.756 --> 01:20:44.553
They are merely food.

607
01:20:45.356 --> 01:20:46.675
Akasha. please... .

608
01:20:46.876 --> 01:20:49.788
You think you can change my will?

609
01:20:50.436 --> 01:20:53.269
l've had enough of this discussion.

610
01:20:53.476 --> 01:20:54.955
Join me or die.

611
01:20:55.396 --> 01:20:56.954
l will not.

612
01:20:57.156 --> 01:20:58.874
- L will not.
- L will not.

613
01:20:59.076 --> 01:21:00.589
l will not.

614
01:21:08.436 --> 01:21:09.835
Do you love me?

615
01:21:11.636 --> 01:21:14.230
- Yes.
- Then prove it.

616
01:21:16.276 --> 01:21:17.629
Kill her.

617
01:21:18.676 --> 01:21:21.634
- She's nothing to me.
- Just the same...

618
01:21:22.596 --> 01:21:24.826
...l'd like for you to kill her.

619
01:21:28.556 --> 01:21:33.391
- You will not touch her!
- You still think to challenge me?!

620
01:21:36.596 --> 01:21:40.384
- Now.
- No. it's all right. Aunt Maharet.

621
01:21:41.156 --> 01:21:43.033
lt's what l want.

622
01:21:49.156 --> 01:21:51.226
How sweet.

623
01:21:57.156 --> 01:21:58.669
l'm ready.

624
01:23:12.356 --> 01:23:14.347
See. my children?

625
01:23:15.476 --> 01:23:17.944
Remember your real family!

626
01:23:19.236 --> 01:23:20.794
Or join hers.

627
01:23:21.996 --> 01:23:23.509
Now...

628
01:23:25.356 --> 01:23:27.074
...give me my crown.

629
01:23:28.716 --> 01:23:30.786
Spoken like a true king.

630
01:23:33.836 --> 01:23:35.428
Come.

631
01:23:45.156 --> 01:23:48.432
You see how he obeys?

632
01:23:48.836 --> 01:23:50.110
You will...

633
01:23:51.076 --> 01:23:53.590
...or you will all die.

634
01:23:59.076 --> 01:24:00.828
That is enough. Lestat.

635
01:24:10.356 --> 01:24:12.187
That is enough. Lestat! Stop!

636
01:25:17.516 --> 01:25:19.871
You kill me...

637
01:25:20.076 --> 01:25:22.988
...you kill yourselves.

638
01:26:06.236 --> 01:26:07.954
Wait. Lestat.

639
01:26:10.636 --> 01:26:12.035
You must stop.

640
01:28:40.676 --> 01:28:43.748
She drank Akasha's last drop.

641
01:28:45.116 --> 01:28:48.825
She took Akasha's death into herself.

642
01:28:50.156 --> 01:28:51.748
She's not dead.

643
01:28:52.636 --> 01:28:54.672
She sleeps.

644
01:29:50.876 --> 01:29:52.389
Hello?

645
01:30:23.796 --> 01:30:25.468
Oh. my God!

646
01:30:26.276 --> 01:30:27.755
Jesse?

647
01:30:28.836 --> 01:30:30.235
Hello. David.

648
01:30:41.436 --> 01:30:43.472
David. this is Lestat.

649
01:30:44.036 --> 01:30:47.870
- Hello.
- L have something for you.

650
01:30:51.596 --> 01:30:53.268
l believe...

651
01:30:53.556 --> 01:30:56.150
...that you wanted this back.

652
01:30:58.196 --> 01:31:01.825
Yes. thank you. Thank you so much.

653
01:31:11.716 --> 01:31:13.468
- Can l ask...?
- What's it like?

654
01:31:15.036 --> 01:31:17.231
Do you want to find out?

655
01:31:18.196 --> 01:31:19.629
Me?

656
01:31:19.836 --> 01:31:22.350
No. l'm too old to live forever.

657
01:31:22.676 --> 01:31:25.474
Well. if you ever change your mind... .

658
01:31:28.196 --> 01:31:29.914
So this is goodbye.

659
01:31:30.836 --> 01:31:32.110
Yes.

660
01:32:28.916 --> 01:32:30.827
Hello. David.

661
01:37:25.636 --> 01:37:26.625
Subtitles by
SDl Media Group

662
01:37:26.796 --> 01:37:27.785
[ENGLlSH]
